__pycache__/
*.pyc

# .foundry/ runtime-partition rationale retained after the default-deny block below subsumed the
# per-file rules that used to encode it (scripts/foundry-apply-runtime-gitignore.sh; AC-RGLS-5):
# - .foundry/authz-ledger.jsonl (AC-ELM-4 / ER #211 housekeeping): the delegable-authorization-
#   envelope's real, append-only runtime authorization ledger (A7) must never be accidentally
#   committed to a code repo.
# - .foundry/per-worker-env/: worker env allocation records carry full argv captures that may
#   embed flag-passed secrets.

# FOUNDRY-RUNTIME-GITIGNORE-BEGIN (managed by scripts/foundry-apply-runtime-gitignore.sh -- do not edit by hand)
# .foundry/ runtime partitions are ignored by default; the designed-tracked set is re-included.
/.foundry/*
!/.foundry/README.md
!/.foundry/build-provenance.yaml
!/.foundry/stack-profile.lock
# FOUNDRY-RUNTIME-GITIGNORE-END (re-run the applier to converge; do not edit by hand)

# Local deviation from the shipped default (AC-RGLS-7): build-provenance.yaml co-carry snapshots
# written here are regenerable and declared in no contract's allowed_paths; committing them lands
# unattributed files (ER #167). This pattern is re-emitted after the managed block below because
# git resolves the LAST matching pattern, so it must win over the block's re-include.
.foundry/build-provenance.yaml
